    "dateRange": {},
    "description": "GenAPA, a UAAO (United Asian American Organizations)-organized event, has been a proud tradition on the University of Michigan campus since 1995. As one of the largest and best student-run pan-Asian cultural programs in the nation, GenAPA consistently attracts nearly 200 participants along with a culturally diverse audience. It showcases the unity and strength of the Asian/Pacific Islander American community by alluding to the past while collectively moving the whole community into the future. Promoting cultural diversity through tradition and history remains intrinsic to the core values of GenAPA. Each year it strives to improve its program while preserving the cultural foundation upon which it was built."
